Q)Prime number
n = int(input('Enter any Number : '))
for i in range(2, n // 2 + 1):
    if n % i == 0:
        print(f'{n} is not a prime number')
        break
else:
    print(f'{n} is prime number')

-Here, Loop runs from 2 to n/2
-If n is a prime number then it runs n/2 times
-So Time Complexity is O(n/2)
-Ignore constant so Time Complexity is O(n)

Common Complexities:
Complexity    Meaning    Example
O(1)         Constant    Access element
O(n)          Linear     Loop
O(n²)        Quadratic   Nested loops
O(log n)     Logarithmic Binary Search
O(n log n)   Logarithmic MergeSort, Quick Sort
O(n³)        Cubic3      Nested loops, Matrix problems
O(2ⁿ)       Exponential   Recursion, Fibonacci
O(n!)       Factorial     Permutations, very slow

-Order of Growth: O(1) < O(log n) < O(n) < O(n log n) < O(n²) < O(n³) < O(2ⁿ) < O(n!)

